{"id":12541,"date":"2025-04-07T10:48:34","date_gmt":"2025-04-07T10:48:34","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/invitation-to-the-workshop-infrared-nanoscopy-of-soft-materials\/"},"modified":"2025-04-07T10:48:34","modified_gmt":"2025-04-07T10:48:34","slug":"invitation-to-the-workshop-infrared-nanoscopy-of-soft-materials","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/invitation-to-the-workshop-infrared-nanoscopy-of-soft-materials\/","title":{"rendered":"Invitation to the workshop Infrared Nanoscopy of Soft Materials"},"content":{"rendered":"<p class=\"\" data-start=\"298\" data-end=\"635\">Dear customers! We cordially invite you to a unique analytical workshop focused on nanoscopy at KTH \u2013 Royal Institute of Technology in Stockholm, in collaboration with <a href=\"https:\/\/www.attocube.com\/en\/business-sectors\/nanoscale-analytics\"><strong>Attocube Systems<\/strong><\/a> (<a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/ir-neascopes\/\">Neaspec<\/a>). This workshop is a unique opportunity to meet top scientists who were at the origin of infrared nanoscopy and are now using it in a wide range of research areas. <\/p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"637\" data-end=\"879\">In addition, you will have the opportunity to <strong data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"714\">measure your own samples for free<\/strong>. You can use these sessions to inspire new projects, grant applications, publications, and establish new friendships and collaborations. <\/p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"188\" data-end=\"291\"><strong data-start=\"191\" data-end=\"231\">KTH, Stockholm, 20. \u2013 May 21, 2025<\/strong><br data-start=\"231\" data-end=\"234\"><strong data-start=\"237\" data-end=\"291\">Measuring your samples: 22. \u2013 May 23, 2025<\/strong><\/p>\n<h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"886\" data-end=\"918\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"918\">Main points of the program:<\/strong><\/span><\/h3>\n<ul data-start=\"920\" data-end=\"1349\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"920\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"922\" data-end=\"1025\"><strong data-start=\"922\" data-end=\"943\">Introductory lectures<\/strong>: Inspiring presentations by experts in AFM, IR and infrared nanoscopy<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1106\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1106\"><strong data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1044\">Live demonstration<\/strong>: NanoIR demonstration on biomaterials and polymer samples<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1107\" data-end=\"1212\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1109\" data-end=\"1212\"><strong data-start=\"1109\" data-end=\"1129\">Poster section<\/strong>: Space for discussion on the application of infrared nanoscopy to your research projects<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1213\" data-end=\"1349\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1215\" data-end=\"1349\"><strong data-start=\"1215\" data-end=\"1246\">Interactive sample measurement<\/strong>: Bring your own sample and take part in a <strong data-start=\"1290\" data-end=\"1319\">free hands-on measurement<\/strong> (prior reservation required)<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"1356\" data-end=\"1380\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong data-start=\"1363\" data-end=\"1380\">Event details:<\/strong><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1382\" data-end=\"1455\"><strong data-start=\"1382\" data-end=\"1399\">Venue<\/strong>: KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Stockholm, Sweden<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"\" data-start=\"1462\" data-end=\"1481\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Registration fee:<\/strong><\/span><\/h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1483\" data-end=\"1652\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1483\" data-end=\"1532\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1532\"><strong data-start=\"1485\" data-end=\"1524\">Early bird registration until April 30th: <\/strong> 150 \u20ac<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"1533\" data-end=\"1652\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1652\"><strong data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1574\">Standard registration after April 30th: <\/strong> 200 \u20ac<br data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1583\"><em data-start=\"1583\" data-end=\"1652\">(the price includes refreshments, lunches for both days of the workshop and a conference dinner)<\/em><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<figure id=\"attachment_9779\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-9779\" style=\"width: 600px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9779\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/22fa6be1-300x257.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"513\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/22fa6be1-300x257.jpg 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/22fa6be1-1024x876.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/22fa6be1-768x657.jpg 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/12\/22fa6be1.jpg 1150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-9779\" class=\"wp-caption-text\"><a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/ir-neascopefs\/\"><strong>IR-neascope+fs<\/strong><\/a>, one of the modular SNOM microscopes from <strong>Attocube <\/strong>(formerly Neaspec)<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Dear customers! We cordially invite you to a unique analytical workshop focused on nanoscopy at KTH \u2013 Royal Institute of Technology in Stockholm, in collaboration with Attocube Systems (Neaspec). This workshop is a unique opportunity to meet top scientists who were at the origin of infrared nanoscopy and are now using it in a wide [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":12538,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[135,33],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-12541","post","type-p